1
00:00:10,771 --> 00:00:10,931
Verse 1

2
00:00:10,931 --> 00:00:15,798
We were seventeen in orchestra, tuning violins and hearts,

3
00:00:15,798 --> 00:00:20,824
You whispered meeps and murps at me, and somehow that was the start.

4
00:00:20,824 --> 00:00:25,691
You’d walk me home past the bleachers, tuck me in like it was art,

5
00:00:25,691 --> 00:00:30,080
And I swear I knew right then you’d be the boy I’d never part from.

6
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:30,319
Pre‑Chorus

7
00:00:30,319 --> 00:00:35,426
Now mornings feel too quiet, no duck‑hair smile in sight,

8
00:00:35,426 --> 00:00:40,293
And the bike built for two is waiting in the garage like it knows I miss you.

9
00:00:40,293 --> 00:00:40,372
Chorus

10
00:00:40,372 --> 00:00:45,239
But I’m counting down to December,

11
00:00:45,239 --> 00:00:49,309
Every sunrise pulls me closer.

12
00:00:49,309 --> 00:00:51,543
Spain feels like a world away,

13
00:00:51,543 --> 00:00:55,213
But you’re still my midnight caller.

14
00:00:55,213 --> 00:00:57,846
And I get annoyed when you speak Spanish—

15
00:00:57,846 --> 00:01:00,239
You’ll get better, I just know it—

16
00:01:00,239 --> 00:01:04,388
But I’ll forgive you when I see you,

17
00:01:04,388 --> 00:01:06,862
’Cause I’m counting down to December.

18
00:01:06,862 --> 00:01:16,750
Verse 2

19
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:21,569
You send me pictures of the plazas, sunlight dripping off the stones,

20
00:01:21,622 --> 00:01:26,729
I send you voice notes full of teasing, but it’s hard sleeping alone.

21
00:01:26,729 --> 00:01:31,676
I ride our tandem down the driveway, pretend your hands are on my own,

22
00:01:31,676 --> 00:01:35,984
And I laugh imagining your morning face, half‑awake and duck‑tone.

23
00:01:35,984 --> 00:01:36,303
Pre‑Chorus

24
00:01:36,303 --> 00:01:41,011
I keep your sweater on my pillow, it’s the closest thing to you,

25
00:01:41,011 --> 00:01:45,798
And I swear the threads remember every meep and murp we ever used.

26
00:01:45,798 --> 00:01:45,957
Chorus

27
00:01:45,957 --> 00:01:50,984
But I’m counting down to December,

28
00:01:50,984 --> 00:01:54,973
Every sunrise pulls me closer.

29
00:01:54,973 --> 00:01:57,128
Spain feels like a world away,

30
00:01:57,128 --> 00:02:00,798
But you’re still my midnight caller.

31
00:02:00,798 --> 00:02:03,431
And I get annoyed when you speak Spanish—

32
00:02:03,431 --> 00:02:05,904
You’ll get better, I just know it—

33
00:02:05,904 --> 00:02:09,894
But I’ll forgive you when I see you,

34
00:02:09,894 --> 00:02:12,128
’Cause I’m counting down to December.

35
00:02:12,128 --> 00:02:17,314
Bridge

36
00:02:17,314 --> 00:02:19,787
Maybe love is just a language

37
00:02:19,787 --> 00:02:22,261
We invented in that classroom,

38
00:02:22,261 --> 00:02:24,894
Something sweeter than the phrases

39
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:27,207
You’re practicing in Madrid.

40
00:02:27,207 --> 00:02:29,761
And when I land and you run toward me,

41
00:02:29,761 --> 00:02:33,670
I’ll forget the months without you—

42
00:02:33,670 --> 00:02:36,144
’Cause every mile was just a promise

43
00:02:36,144 --> 00:02:44,133
That December always kept.

